# Put this file’s variables in `.env` here at the REPO ROOT (next to package.json).
# Do NOT put EXPO_PUBLIC_* in back-end/.env — the API never reads those; Expo/Metro only loads root `.env`.

# Physical phone (Expo Go) or when emulator defaults are wrong — use your PC’s IP on the SAME network as the phone (no trailing slash):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.5:4000

# Windows hotspot: the PC is usually NOT your Wi‑Fi IP. In PowerShell run `ipconfig` and use the IPv4
# on the hotspot / “Local Area Connection*” adapter (often 192.168.137.1), then restart Expo with cache clear.

# Physical device + Expo Go: if Metro shows exp://127.0.0.1, run `npm run start:phone` instead of `npx expo start`
# (it sets REACT_NATIVE_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME from the host above).

# Public registration / verify-email: configure outbound SMTP and EMAIL_VERIFICATION_APP_URL in `back-end/.env`
# (see that file’s comments). The deep link base should open your app’s `verify-email` route (https or exp://).
